I believe you.

And there’s an important distinction between having the stomach for something, having the appetite for it, and choosing to do it.

You can understand brutality without celebrating it. You can endure things you wish nobody had to endure. And you can be capable of something without wanting that capability to define you.

Sometimes the unfortunate part is knowing exactly what you’re capable of.

The question becomes not what you can stomach, but what you believe is worth swallowing.